Source-facing, not provider-facing
----------------------------------

Captured source declarations and generated projections are build-time and
runtime facts about the provider's interface. They are not execution evidence,
not account-scope evidence and not live provider certification. Controlled
GitHub-compatible responses remain fake evidence; live account evidence
requires separate authorization and its own receipts.

Supplemental official documentation capture
-------------------------------------------

The pinned OpenAPI capture above declares no `security` scheme and no
`securitySchemes` at all, so the compiled operation was unauthenticated *by
declaration*. Missing OpenAPI metadata is not evidence of anonymous-only
operation, so the `issues/list-for-repo` operation admits one separately
provenanced official documentation capture as a second, non-OpenAPI document:

  source_id:    github-docs-rest-authentication
  dialect:      official-documentation   (never parsed as YAML or JSON, no
                                         closure, addressable only by an exact
                                         byte range "#bytes:<start>-<end>")
  url:          https://docs.github.com/en/rest/authentication/authenticating-to-the-rest-api
  retrieved:    2026-09-19T12:43:59Z
  byte length:  345525
  sha256:       24bf2e4f9e61946a68e52f5436ef7310aaaca390a22ada441dd1f4ed38bd9d66
  retained at:  connectors/github/official-documentation/documents/authenticating-to-the-rest-api.html
  capture copy: connectors/github/captures/github-docs-rest-authentication (byte-identical)
  license:      Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
                (c) GitHub, Inc. / GitHub Docs, retained at
                connectors/github/official-documentation/documents/github-docs-LICENSE.txt
                (18,620 bytes, SHA-256 12d3a82a7d1378e6f597ec23d63a081aeb6ec4bc8de2a76ee9dc96c34c6d7a1b)

Only the admitted operation may cite it, and only for the credential channel
that the description does not declare. The three witness ranges, each resolved
against the retained bytes with `python3 verify.py` locators, are:

  #bytes:226676-226922  "sending the token in the Authorization header of
                        your request" (documented request-header placement)
  #bytes:227630-227854  "you can use Authorization: Bearer or Authorization:
                        token to pass a token ... a JSON web token (JWT) must
                        use Authorization: Bearer"
  #bytes:226923-227157  the documented code sample that sends
                        --header "Authorization: Bearer YOUR-TOKEN" to
                        https://api.github.com

The admitted channel is `authorization` (header `Authorization`, prefix
`Bearer `, audience `https://api.github.com`). It is declared **optional**,
because the retained operation page states that the endpoint "can be used
without authentication ... if only public resources are requested"; a
supplemental fact may add a credential channel, never mandate one, and the
requirement that *this* private connection present a server-held credential is
PM connection policy, not a provider protocol fact. The channel is resolved by
the credential boundary: its binding is secret and never appears in a public
command, catalog entry or CLI flag.

Precedence, refusal and scope
-----------------------------

OpenAPI remains authoritative for everything it declares, and the supplemental
fact may only add what it does not declare. Refused by construction: a channel
created from OpenAPI description bytes (even bytes that contain the channel
words), a witness that does not resolve to retained bytes, a range that names
neither the declared header nor the declared scheme, a mandatory created
channel, a widened or rewritten origin, a rewritten fixed header, and any
operation other than `issues/list-for-repo`. The capture, its manifest, its
retrieval script and its verifier under
`connectors/github/official-documentation/` are untouched by this admission and
remain the evidence of record.

